<title>USA: Union Pacific to join Mexico rail bid - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Union Pacific to join Mexico rail bid - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Pacific Corp plans to join a consortium bidding for a busy Mexican rail line, the Wall Street Journal said in Wednesday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>The U.S. railroad will make a bid with Mexican construction firm Ingernieros Civiles Asociados and mining company Grupo Mexico SA for a 4,000-mile Pacific-North rail line, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The Journal said the bid size had not yet been determined.</p>
<p>U.S. railroads are battling for stakes in Mexico's national transportation system which is finally being privatised after years of government control, it said.</p>
